; Axis C (exclusive-group presence) — schema-ambiguity case.
;
; The `phrase` form requires exactly one of `:loops` or `:events`, but
; *both* keys carry literal defaults (empty vector). The author writes
; neither. With the group-aware rule, no alt is author-present and
; multiple alts are default-only -> the schema is ambiguous (defaults
; alone admit more than one path). This is *not* a document error —
; it points the schema author at the conflicting defaults.
;
; Diagnostic: `multiple_defaulted_alternatives_in_group` at `[phrase]`.
; See `docs/plans/exclusive-group-default-semantics.md`.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name phrase
    (key :name loops :type vector :default [] :optional true)
    (key :name events :type vector :default [] :optional true)
    (exclusive-group :cardinality exactly-one
      (alt :keys [loops])
      (alt :keys [events]))))

(phrase)
